│ appname.Picking.origin" indicates that       │
│ Django is not correctly recognizing the      │
│ parent_link=True attribute on the origin     │
│ OneToOneField in the Picking model. This is  │
│ likely because Django’s ORM isn’t properly   │
│ handling the parent-child relationship       │
│ defined by parent_link=True.  The core issue │
│ is that Django’s internal mechanisms for     │
│ managing parent-child relationships aren’t   │
│ being utilized correctly when                │
│ parent_link=True is set.  The simplest and   │
│ most robust solution is to explicitly set    │
│ parent_link=True on the document_ptr field,  │
│ ensuring that Django’s ORM correctly manages │
│ the relationship.                            │
│                                              │
│ Patch:                                       │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 1              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file][file]models.py[/file]                │
│  [original]class Picking(Document):\n        │
│  origin = models.OneToOneField(Document,     │
│  related_name='picking',                     │
│  on_delete=models.PROTECT)[/original]        │
│  [patched]class Picking(Document):\n         │
│  origin = models.OneToOneField(Document,     │
│  related_name='picking',                     │
│  on_delete=models.PROTECT,                   │
│  parent_link=True)[/patched]                 │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│ ┏━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┓ │
│ ┃              modification 2              ┃ │
│ ┗━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━┛ │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│  [file][file]models.py[/file]                │
│  [original]class Document(models.Model):\n   │
│  pass\n\nclass Picking(Document):\n          │
│  document_ptr =                              │
│  models.OneToOneField(Document,              │
│  on_delete=models.CASCADE, parent_link=True  │
│  related_name='+')\n    origin =             │
│  models.OneToOneField(Document,              │
│  related_name='picking',                     │
│  on_delete=models.PROTECT)[/original]        │
│  [patched]class Document(models.Model):\n    │
│  pass\n\nclass Picking(Document):\n          │
│  document_ptr =                              │
│  models.OneToOneField(Document,              │
│  on_delete=models.CASCADE, parent_link=True  │
│  related_name='+')\n    origin =             │
│  models.OneToOneField(Document,              │
│  related_name='picking',                     │
│  on_delete=models.PROTECT,                   │
│  parent_link=True)[/patched]                 │
│                                              │
│                                              │
│ The patch adds parent_link=True to the       │
│ origin OneToOneField in the Picking model.   │
│ This ensures that Django’s ORM correctly     │
│ handles the parent-child relationship. I've  │
│ also added it to the document_ptr field for  │
│ consistency.                                 │
