│ The issue stems from the document_ptr and    │
│ origin fields both being OneToOneFields      │
│ referencing the Document model. Django’s     │
│ parent_link=True option, when used with      │
│ on_delete=models.CASCADE, can lead to        │
│ conflicts when multiple OneToOneFields point │
│ to the same parent. Specifically, the origin │
│ field’s on_delete=models.PROTECT is causing  │
│ the ImproperlyConfigured error.  PROTECT     │
│ prevents deletion of the parent, but doesn’t │
│ inherently resolve the issue of multiple     │
│ references. The simplest and most robust     │
│ solution is to change the on_delete behavior │
│ of the origin field to models.CASCADE as     │
│ well, mirroring the behavior of              │
│ document_ptr. This ensures that if the       │
│ parent document is deleted, the origin field │
│ is also deleted, resolving the conflict.     │
